# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Kohei Numata et al. (2026). Quantum machine learning interatomic potential: Application of variational quantum algorithm.
#   arXiv (Cornell University). doi:10.48550/arxiv.2607.27841  arXiv:2607.27841v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2607.27841v1 (sha256 e4aacd948fb18e10...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 682 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/numata2026.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: TorchANI models pre-trained classically and then
# transferred with a variational quantum circuit (or, for comparison, a
# classical layer) inserted between the input and output networks, on the
# D1 subset (one non-hydrogen atom) of the ANI data; encoded results are
# the stated mean test RMSEs for nq = 4 and 12 with the RzRy circuit and
# the classical layer. Cholesterol isomer tests and other circuit settings
# are figure-only.

